@node Testing
@section Testing

@command{make check} runs a unit test per module (RFC vectors where they
exist), loopback tests that pair engines and connections over a
simulated network with a virtual clock (loss, reordering, duplication,
corruption, NAT rebinding), and interoperability scripts against
independent implementations: @file{tests/interop.sh} (TLS against OpenSSL
and GnuTLS), @file{tests/interop-dtls.sh} and @file{tests/interop-dtls12.sh}
(DTLS against wolfSSL, OpenSSL and GnuTLS) and @file{tests/interop-quic.sh}
(QUIC against quiche: handshakes, loss, Retry, Version Negotiation, key
update, migration, DATAGRAM, 0-RTT and concurrent clients, both
directions).  Scripts skip themselves (exit 77) when their peers are
missing; set @env{GQ_NO_INTEROP} to skip them, @env{GQ_INTEROP_FILTER} to
run scenarios whose names contain a string, and @env{QUICHE_DIR} to name
the directory holding @command{quiche-client} and @command{quiche-server}.
The library is also run under AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.

